# AI Agent — Trace-First Workflow

## TFW Routing

This project uses Trace-First Workflow. Treat `.tfw/` as the source of truth.

Load new-session context in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `.tfw/conventions.md`
3. `.tfw/glossary.md`
4. `KNOWLEDGE.md` if present
5. `README.md` Task Board
6. Relevant HL, TS, RF, REVIEW, and implementation files

Use repository-local Codex skills from `.agents/skills/tfw-*/SKILL.md`. Invoke them with `$tfw-*`; treat `/tfw-*` as a soft text alias.

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `$tfw-plan` | Plan HL/TS |
| `$tfw-research` | Produce research traces and RES |
| `$tfw-handoff` | Execute approved TS and write ONB/RF |
| `$tfw-review` | Verify RF and write REVIEW |
| `$tfw-resume` | Build task/phase status |
| `$tfw-docs` | Update knowledge index and tech debt |
| `$tfw-knowledge` | Consolidate Fact Candidates |
| `$tfw-release` | Prepare a release |
| `$tfw-update` | Upgrade the local framework |
| `$tfw-config` | Audit or change synchronized config |
| `$tfw-init` | Initialize TFW |

Each skill must read its canonical file in `.tfw/workflows/`, enforce that workflow's role lock and gates, use canonical `.tfw/templates/`, and stop at the workflow hard stop.

Reply in the user's latest language. Be direct, precise, and complete. Do not use placeholders or request plain-text secrets.
